# Episode — Computational Possibility: Destructive Audit, Derived Calculus, and Positive Reconstruction


## Identity

- date: `2026-08-19`
- truthRole: `manual-curated-research-process-memory`
- owner: `research-owner:computational-possibility`
- standing: `CURRENT_REUNDERSTANDING_CYCLE_COMPLETE`

This episode begins **after** Computational Possibility Project Formation v0.1 had already closed. It records a later decision to reopen understanding without automatically reopening architecture.

It complements the earlier episode `2026-08-18-19-computational-possibility-formation-currentness-and-repair.md`.


### Hostile cases

The audit tested:

- pointwise versus uniform quantification;
- adversarial alternation;
- randomized probability scope;
- private/public randomness visibility;
- interactive roles;
- family quantification;
- discoverability versus existence.


## Transition 10 — Runtime / Interlocus applicability dogfood

A live route/profile outage plus a successful local Runtime witness created a three-way applicability split:

- narrow constructive actual witness -> bounded `APPLIES`;
- exact capability premise unavailable/currentness drift -> no current `APPLIES`, older basis may be `EXPIRED`;
- broad system-wide impossibility without exhaustive candidate coverage -> `UNRESOLVED`.

Surviving practical laws:

- `HistoricalCapability != CurrentCapability`;
- `ExactRouteUnavailable != GlobalNetworkImpossibility`;
- `OneRouteFailure != ActualCandidateCoverage`.

This was direct real-owner evidence for the constructive/impossibility directional asymmetry in Applicability.


## Process-level lessons

- project formation does not imply the best explanatory model has already been found;
- a thin primitive core can support a very rich relational theory;
- hostile tests should target quantifier/dependency/composition/transport structure, not just primitive nouns;
- temporary audit lenses should be deleted or demoted before canonicalization;
- consumer dogfood can justify an independent research owner's value without forcing that owner to absorb downstream engineering truth;
- a real scoped failure is often evidence for a narrower claim, not a global impossibility theorem;
- positive reconstruction should follow destructive audit before expanding engineering materialization.

# Episode — Research Understanding, Durable Synthesis, and Anti-Rediscovery


## Identity

- dateRange: `2026-08-18/19`
- truthRole: `manual-curated-research-process-memory`
- upstreamCollection: `synthesis/2026-08-18-19-research-understanding/`
- standing: `HISTORICAL_PROCESS_CURRENTLY_USEFUL`


## Pressure that exposed the gap

During a broad research review/explanation conversation, high-value understanding emerged **between** owner results:

- a compact responsibility/worldview map across Reality, Meaning, Possibility, Cognition, Realization, Work, Synthesis, Map, Investigation and Current Truth;
- a human-readable compression of the research method;
- owner-topology explanation showing why truth-condition ownership differs from repository partitioning;
- a Host/Harness/Runtime/domain-result realization guide;
- a research-significance map separating world-model change, method change, formalization and frontier value;
- a Human–Ordivon learning/knowledge-placement map;
- explicit anti-rediscovery rules for checking prior results before opening fresh research;
- an assimilation manifest distinguishing what was already durable, newly synthesized, useful explanation, and deliberately not copied.

Much of the underlying truth was already durable upstream, but the **semantic compression itself** was not. Reconstructing it required repeatedly reading many owners and re-deriving the relationships.


## New tension discovered

Even after the richer assimilation pass, one important class remained underrepresented: **research-process history**.

Publication history or a synthesis manifest can tell us that an authority or understanding changed. It does not necessarily tell us:

- what the old belief was;
- why it was reasonable;
- what hostile case attacked it;
- which evidence changed the standing;
- what survived the repair;
- whether an old instruction became stale because it was wrong, or because the world/currentness changed.

That gap motivates the present `research-process-lineage/` manual layer.


## Current standing

The existing `synthesis/2026-08-18-19-research-understanding/` collection is current as non-authoritative curated synthesis, subject to revalidation if upstream owners materially advance.

The process-lineage extension is an experiment/manual requirement, not yet an Atlas schema or generated view.

