The remaining frontier is capability, not theory:

> Can a bounded Agent, from naturally changing owner/world evidence plus existing plural mandates and owner boundaries, formulate—or correctly decline—a new decision-relevant research pressure before a human supplies the exact problem, and validate it through later owner-admitted decision-changing probes rather than hidden labels or self-score?

F17 is the current prospective owner-native test of this capability. It is unresolved because only natural no-op/control events have occurred so far.


## 7. Host persistence utility — design-ready, not admitted

A possible future natural experiment would compare:

- `CHECKPOINT_REVALIDATE`: exact frozen WorkingCheckpoint plus current owner revalidation;
- `FRESH_OWNER_REOBSERVE`: same original objective/work identity and bounded canonical owner locators, but no retained derived findings.

