A four-quadrant hostile matrix established that pressure correctness and solution-generation quality are independent: the right problem can have poor options, and an irrelevant problem can have excellent options.

Prior-art subtraction again removed the universal-theory claim. Problem finding/formulation, problemistic search, opportunity discovery/creation, scientific problem choice, interest-versus-feasibility, active learning/experiment design, and portfolio allocation already cover the component distinctions. Current autonomous-science systems also automate substantial downstream research after a supplied topic/research objective.


